.TH APERI-SESSION 1 2026-11-15 "aperi @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aperi-session \- session helper for aperi
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aperi-session
.RI [ option ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aperi-session
is a small daemon meant to be started at the beginning of the graphical
session, by the
.B aperi-session.service
systemd user unit or by the compositor.
It provides two features, each of which can be disabled:
.TP
.B fm1
A minimal implementation of the
.B org.freedesktop.FileManager1
D-Bus service, used for example by browsers to show a downloaded file in
its folder.
Only the
.B ShowItems
method is implemented: for every
.B file://
URI it receives,
.B aperi-session
runs
.PP
.RS
.RS
.B aperi aperi-show-items://\c
.I percent-encoded-path
.RE
.PP
so that the request can be handled by an
.B aperi-show-items://
rule in the
.BR aperi (1)
configuration.
The program is fully detached from
.B aperi-session
and inherits its environment.
.RE
.TP
.B wipewine
Removal of the
.I wine-extension*.desktop
and
.I wine-protocol*.desktop
files that wine creates in
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/applications ,
both those present at startup and the new ones, as soon as they are
created.
These files make wine programs the default applications for common file
types.
.PP
Only one instance per user can run: a second one prints a message and
exits with status 0.
.B aperi-session
reports its readiness to systemd (the unit has
.BR Type=notify )
and exits cleanly on
.BR SIGTERM ,
.B SIGINT
and
.BR SIGHUP .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-no\-fm1
Don't provide the org.freedesktop.FileManager1 service.
It is always disabled if aperi was built without D-Bus support.
.TP
.BR \-W ", " \-\-no\-wipewine
Don't remove the wine file association desktop files.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-exit\-with\-session
Exit when the Wayland compositor
.RB ( $WAYLAND_DISPLAY )
terminates, so that
.B aperi-session
doesn't outlive the session when it's started by the compositor.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory of the applications directory watched by wipewine
.RI ( ~/.local/share
if not set).
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Directory of the single instance lock file and, with
.BR \-\-exit\-with\-session ,
of the Wayland socket.
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
The Wayland socket watched with
.BR \-\-exit\-with\-session .
.TP
.B PATH
Used to find
.B aperi
and, through it, the programs handling ShowItems requests.
.TP
.B NOTIFY_SOCKET
Set by systemd to receive the readiness notification.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @SYSTEMDUSERUNITDIR@/aperi-session.service
The systemd user unit.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/aperi-session.lock
The single instance lock file
.RI ( /tmp/aperi-session- uid .lock
if
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
is not set).
.TP
.I @DATADIR@/doc/aperi/examples/show_items.py
An example handler for
.B aperi-show-items://
URIs: it copies the path to the clipboard and opens a terminal in the
folder containing the file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when terminated by a signal, when the compositor exits with
.BR \-\-exit\-with\-session ,
or when another instance is already running; 1 on errors, including the
loss of the session bus connection or of the watched directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start it with the systemd user unit, which requires a session that starts
.BR graphical-session.target :
.PP
.RS
.EX
systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now aperi-session.service
.EE
.RE
.PP
To pass options, override
.B ExecStart
with
.BR "systemctl \-\-user edit aperi-session.service" :
.PP
.RS
.EX
[Service]
ExecStart=
ExecStart=@BINDIR@/aperi-session \-\-no\-wipewine
.EE
.RE
.PP
Without systemd, start it from the sway configuration:
.PP
.RS
.EX
exec aperi-session \-\-exit\-with\-session
.EE
.RE
.PP
A rule in the aperi configuration to handle ShowItems requests:
.PP
.RS
.EX
aperi-show-items://=show_items.py
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aperi (1),
.BR aperi-setup (1),
.BR systemd.unit (5)
.SH AUTHORS
Matteo Beniamino <m.beniamino@tautologica.org>
